# Case 1
  Problem :
  - computer dosen't start and after working 2-3 days it dosen't start
  Solution :
  - change the cosmos battery (in older laptop), newer versions are operated from the main bettery
  Learning :
  - after changing the battery and reconnect the main battery in HP and Dell Laptops it got restart 3 times if you don't let it restart it will directly damage the IC
  - after reconnect the bettery HP and Dell leptop get different beeps for different problem,
    if you got a beep 3 times listen it carefully and decode it, some normal fixes that may be ram loose or any general issue.
  
  Concept :
  - A "cosmos" cell (better known as a CMOS battery) is a small, flat, coin-shaped battery on your motherboard. It looks like an oversized watch battery
    What it Does,
      Saves Time    : It keeps your computer's date and time running accurately even when the PC is unplugged
      Saves Settings: It stores your Basic Input/Output System (BIOS) settings, such as your boot order and hardware configurations
      Analogy       : Think of it like a watch. Just like a watch keeps ticking when you take it off,
                    Tthe CMOS battery keeps your computer's "memory" alive when the PC has no power.

